# Terraform Commands (Quick Revision)

## Initialization

`terraform init`
- Initialize project
- Download providers/modules
- Configure backend

`terraform init -reconfigure`
- Reconfigure backend after changing S3/DynamoDB/backend settings

---

## Validation

`terraform fmt`
- Format Terraform code

`terraform validate`
- Validate Terraform syntax

---

## Planning & Deployment

`terraform plan`
- Preview infrastructure changes

`terraform apply`
- Create or update infrastructure

`terraform destroy`
- Delete infrastructure

---

## Output

`terraform output`
- Display output values

---

## State

`terraform state list`
- List all managed resources

`terraform state show RESOURCE_NAME`
- Show resource details

Example:

`terraform state show aws_instance.web`

`terraform state rm RESOURCE_NAME`
- Remove resource from Terraform state (doesn't delete in AWS)

---

## Workspaces

`terraform workspace list`
- List all workspaces

`terraform workspace new dev`
- Create a workspace

`terraform workspace select dev`
- Switch workspace

`terraform workspace show`
- Show current workspace

`terraform workspace delete dev`
- Delete workspace

---

## Locking

`terraform force-unlock LOCK_ID`
- Remove stale DynamoDB state lock

---

## Import

`terraform import RESOURCE_NAME RESOURCE_ID`

Example:

`terraform import aws_instance.web i-0123456789abcdef0`

- Import existing AWS resource into Terraform

---

## Useful Commands

`terraform version`
- Show Terraform version

`terraform show`
- Show Terraform state

`terraform graph`
- Generate resource dependency graph

---

# Daily Workflow

```
terraform fmt
        ↓
terraform validate
        ↓
terraform init
        ↓
terraform plan
        ↓
terraform apply
        ↓
terraform output
```
